CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ calls: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
no body for callee
--
Members of the partial specialization fn<R(Args...)> defined outside the
class: the definition's parameter pack `Args... args' was counted as one
parameter, so for fn<int()> and fn<int(int, int)> the definition did not
match the member and the member had no body; once matched, the body's
args$0 and args$1 had no parameters of those names.  libc++ defines
std::function's members this way.
